KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ body pack-expansion call expanded to full arity: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.variadic]/5: a pack-expansion use of a function parameter pack in a
function body (here `fp(a...)`, with `a` the parameter pack of `go(A... a)` and
`A` the enclosing class template parameter pack) must expand to one argument per
deduced element.  CBMC expands it to a single argument, so the call is rejected
("wrong number of function arguments: expected 2, but got 1").  This is the
libstdc++ function<_Res(_ArgTypes...)>::operator() body shape
`_M_invoker(_M_functor, std::forward<_ArgTypes>(__args)...)` and is the
remaining blocker for multi-argument std::function invocation (the member
function-pointer type collapse, cpp11_variadic_pack_in_member_funptr_type, is
already fixed).  Flip to CORE once the body pack-expansion uses the full pack
arity.
